.TH INITTAB 5 "2026-02-08" "armybox 0.3.0" "ArmyBox Manual"
.\"
.SH NAME
inittab \- configuration file for armybox init
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I /etc/inittab
file describes which processes are started at bootup and during normal
operation by
.BR armybox-init (8).
.PP
Each line has the format:
.PP
.RS
.IB id : runlevels : action : process
.RE
.PP
Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments.
Blank lines are ignored.
.\"
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.I id
A short identifier for this entry, up to 4 characters.
Conventionally, this is the terminal name without the
.I /dev/
prefix (e.g.,
.BR tty1 ,
.BR ttyS0 ).
The
.I id
field may be empty for entries that don't refer to a specific terminal.
.TP
.I runlevels
This field is present for compatibility with System V init but is
.B ignored
by armybox init.
It may be left empty.
.TP
.I action
Determines when and how the
.I process
is executed.
Valid actions:
.RS
.TP 14
.B sysinit
Executed during system boot, before any
.B wait
or
.B respawn
entries.
All
.B sysinit
entries are run sequentially in order.
.TP
.B wait
Executed once during boot (after
.BR sysinit ).
Init waits for the process to complete before continuing.
.TP
.B once
Executed once during boot, but init does not wait for it to complete.
.TP
.B respawn
The process is started and monitored.
If it exits, init restarts it after a short delay.
This is the standard action for
.BR getty (8)
processes.
.TP
.B askfirst
Like
.BR respawn ,
but before starting the process, init prints the message:
.RS
.PP
.B "Please press Enter to activate this console."
.PP
and waits for the user to press Enter.
Useful for consoles that may not be connected.
.RE
.TP
.B shutdown
Executed during system shutdown (when init receives SIGTERM).
.TP
.B restart
Executed when init receives
.BR SIGHUP .
Typically used to re-exec init itself.
.TP
.B ctrlaltdel
Executed when the Ctrl+Alt+Delete key combination is pressed.
Typically runs
.BR reboot (8).
.RE
.TP
.I process
The command line to execute, including any arguments.
The process is run via
.BR /bin/sh\ \-c
if it contains shell metacharacters; otherwise it is executed directly.
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
A minimal inittab for a serial console system:
.PP
.nf
# Mount essential filesystems
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /dev

# Serial console login
ttyS0::respawn:/sbin/getty -L 115200 ttyS0 vt100

# Reboot on Ctrl-Alt-Delete
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot

# Clean shutdown
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
.fi
.PP
A more complete inittab with multiple consoles:
.PP
.nf
# System initialization
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /dev
::sysinit:/bin/mkdir -p /dev/pts /dev/shm
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devpts devpts /dev/pts
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /dev/shm
::sysinit:/bin/mount -o remount,rw /
::sysinit:/bin/hostname -F /etc/hostname
::sysinit:/sbin/sysctl -p

# Run startup scripts
::wait:/etc/init.d/rcS

# Virtual consoles
tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty1
tty2::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty2
tty3::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty3

# Serial console
ttyS0::respawn:/sbin/getty -L 115200 ttyS0 vt100

# Ctrl-Alt-Delete handler
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot

# Shutdown tasks
::shutdown:/etc/init.d/rcK
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
::shutdown:/sbin/swapoff -a
.fi
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/inittab
The configuration file itself.
.\"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR armybox-init (8),
.BR getty (8),
.BR armybox (1)
.\"
